
§ test

- test (1)
	° check file types and compare values
	° syntax: 
		[ expression ] 
		- or - 
		test expression
	° evaluates expression and returns a status:
		> 0 (true)
		> 1 (false)
	
- external command

- typically located at /usr/bin/[ or /usr/bin/test

- NOTE:
	° spaces
		> requires args and operators to be seperated by spaces 

- [] 
	° same as: 
		test expression

- examples
	° > [ "one" = "one ]
	  > echo $? 

	° > [ 1 -eq 2 ]
	  > echo $? 
	
	° > test "one" = "one"
	  > echo $? 

	° > test 1 -eq 2
	  > echo $? 

- supports various types of tests, including 
	° file tests 
		-e
		-f
		-d
	° string comparisons 
		=
		!=
		-z
		-n
	° numerical comparisons
		-eq
		-ne
		-lt
		-gt
		-le
		-ge

